Chatgpt in helping screen switching code understanding

Local preview
- Open index.html in a browser. No install or build step is needed.
- index.html: all screens, using classes for layout and screen switching.
- includes/styles.css: shared classes, screen layout, belt animation.
- includes/scripts.js: hover, switching screens, filling the form, counting days.
- images/: airport, belt stripes and suitcase exported from the Figma design.

How to test
File a claim → click each fact to fill the matching box → Submit.
The boxes are plain divs, so they cannot be typed into.
The demo follows a fixed order: Declined → Appeal → $300 offer → No → Approved.
Give up and Yes clear the form and return to the airport.
Accept! changes to Accepted and stays on the approved screen.
Each review takes 21 pretend days; the total continues to 42 and 63 days.
In includes/scripts.js, dayLength = 1000 means one real second per day.
Change daysPerReview to change the number of days in each review.

Class examples used as a reference
- Backrooms-with-JS: functions, onclick, style.display, loops, setInterval.
- Color-Planets: event listeners and changing HTML.
- CSS-Planet-Animation: @keyframes and an infinite CSS animation.

Comments starting with //～ mark JS patterns without a matching structure in _Resources.
These include functions with custom parameters, pairing two element lists on click,
splitting digits with %, repeated review rounds, and resetting several boxes on click.
The hover helper also uses mouseleave, which is not in those examples.
